JEV-AI: A Governed Agentic AI Framework for Autonomous Enterprise Automation

Abstract

The rapid advancement of Artificial Intelligence (AI) is transforming enterprise automation from predefined workflows and conversational assistants into intelligent systems capable of reasoning, planning, tool utilization, and autonomous execution. This paper proposes JEV-AI, a governed Agentic AI framework designed to enable secure, scalable, and intelligent automation across complex enterprise environments. The framework combines Large Language Models (LLMs), intent-driven routing, specialized AI agents, enterprise tools, governance controls, and execution observability to create an adaptive automation ecosystem.

JEV-AI introduces an Intent Layer that interprets user requests, identifies operational objectives, and routes tasks to appropriate specialized agents. Instead of relying on an LLM for every processing step, deterministic routing and direct tool execution can be used for predictable operations, reducing unnecessary token consumption, latency, and operational cost. For complex requests, specialized agents dynamically formulate execution plans, select approved tools, invoke APIs or automation workflows, evaluate intermediate results, and determine subsequent actions.

A centralized Tool Registry and Governance Layer manages tool definitions, permissions, parameters, agent-to-tool assignments, versioning, and audit information. This enables organizations to restrict autonomous actions according to security policies while introducing human approval for high-risk operations. A model-independent gateway enables multiple AI models to be evaluated or replaced without redesigning the underlying agent and tool ecosystem. The framework also incorporates comprehensive observability by capturing agent execution traces, tool calls, latency, token utilization, failures, model responses, and execution outcomes.

A Proof of Concept demonstrates JEV-AI through enterprise infrastructure operations in which natural-language requests are converted into controlled actions through intent identification, agent selection, authorized tool execution, result validation, and response generation.

JEV-AI demonstrates how Agentic AI can evolve beyond conversational assistance into a governed, observable, cost-aware, model-independent, and action-oriented enterprise automation platform, while preserving security controls and human oversight for critical operations.
